ller-created owner marker OUTSIDE mysql datadir, strong realpath\/marker\/nonce guards. Root-stage parent private and SOURCE root not data. mysql service runs --user actual Process.uid:Process.gid (host501:20) so host user can remove all stage files; unknown nonroot uid supported via entrypoint. Set --datadir=\/labdata\/data, --tmpdir=\/labdata\/tmp, --socket=\/labdata\/mysql.sock, --pid-file=\/labdata\/mysql.pid, secure-file-priv=NULL; stage\/data initiallyEMPTY, tmp sibling. Public disposable MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD only. This avoids root-owned hostdata requiring unsafe cleanuphelper. On permission failure root will fix before long run; NEVER modify unrelated permissions\/files. One engine at a time: fresh server\/data -> load100M -> (InnoDB: 3 PK-only counts, add k_count(c001), 3 secondary-present counts; MyISAM: 3 PK-only counts) -> clean exit\/reap -> verify ownedcontainer absent -> guarded rm ownstage -> verify host free -> fresh otherengine. Same serverimage\/config\/resources eachstage. Do not overlap tables or engines or reuse previous hostdata. Starting order fixed InnoDB then MyISAM, record orderconfounding. Host capacity preflight >=70GiB perstage, floor12GiB during loader\/counts, capture host+guestFS capacities. Host \/bin\/df -Pk check with safe argv every few seconds while waiting; terminate owned work and cleanup if low; don't prune\/delete unrelated caches\/images\/data or resize VM. Resourcebudget server4GiB\/3CPU, innodb_buffer_pool_size1GiB, key_buffer_size128MiB, innodb_redo_log_capacity1GiB, skiplogbin labonly, defaultdurability otherwise. Overall6h with bounded cleanup120s, perloadstage<=2h\/percount<=20min (set session max_execution_time in lab ifuseful, explicit scope), readiness120s. Every timeout\/failure\/incomplete preserved, not successful; cleanup after failedpartial load alsoownsallresources and data. Do not kill otherbuildkit\/containers.\nDATA: exactly100 columns: id BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, c001..c099 INT NOT NULL, initially no secondary index, no compression\/TDE; add k_count(c001) only for the second InnoDB condition. Same DDL except ENGINE, same deterministicvalues id1..100M and constants1..99 for100intcolumn payload404bytes. Explain fixed-width constant columns, not broad100column\/TDE\/VARCHAR\/LOB generalization. Use server-side SQL INSERT SELECT in100000-row transactions x1000, unique ascending PK; create sharedsmallInnoDB seq100000 via digits crossjoin, no rowgeneration\/clienttransfer. Validate ROW_COUNT()=100000 for EVERY committed batch, accumulatedrows100M and schema100columns\/exactengine. Use mysql CLI persistent stream in ownedserver via docker exec -i, --no-defaults --protocol=SOCKET --socket fixed -uroot -ppubliclabpassword --batch --raw --skip-column-names --unbuffered, connectdeadline. NO per-query subprocess startup inside counttimer. Ruby ownsstdin\/out pipe, start monotonicns beforewrite\/count request, readactualscalar+protocolboundary, retainintegerns; no 3decimal rounding-tozero. For INSERTSELECT execute + SELECT ROW_COUNT() returnscommitted affectedrowcount; no --force, SQLerrors close\/abort with actualexit captured. SQLwrapper marker forvoid\/multirow metadata so errors\/EOF never fabricatedsuccess\/zero. Drainstderr to fullrawlogfile, avoid pipe deadlock; SQL\/clientPID always reaped and recorded. No additional huge validationCOUNT outside3measuredCOUNTs percondition; truth100M from1000actualrowcountreceipts and eachmeasuredCOUNTmust100M (6 counts in InnoDB across2conditions, 3 in MyISAM). Progress every5M elapsed\/rows\/sec\/roughETA, streamedflush; storeall1000batchcounts to resultJSON\/log, no tabledatafiles committed.\nCOUNT: ONLY SELECT COUNT(*) FROM fixedtable, 3 measured runs percondition aftercommittedload orcompletedindexbuild, 9 across3conditions total, no concurrentfixturewrites. Label first post-load vs repeats; no fakecold\/warm since data>bufferpool, OS\/VM\/filecache uncontrolled, postloadflush mayremain. No FLUSH TABLES\/status\/globalcac